; DUT-independent bench machinery: the SPEC-M01 §6.1 protocol monitor, the
; requirements.md §0.6 conservation monitor and the §0.5 octet-time latency
; tagger, with their unit tests on hand-built traces (WO-0009 deliverables 3
; and 4).
;
; No (libraries) field on purpose. Everything here is plain OCaml over the
; standard library and over Stream_word.t, so the monitors need no simulator,
; no Hardcaml and no DUT to be exercised — which is what lets their own tests
; fail when a monitor is wrong instead of when a design is. The one adapter
; that touches a live Axi64 stream lives in test/axi64_probe/ and depends on
; this library, never the other way round.
;
; (pps ppx_expect) alone rather than the ppx_jane set used by
; test/hardcaml_ethernet/dune: [%expect] is the only extension used here, and
; ppx_jane's Base-flavoured operators are deliberately not in scope.

(library
 (name dv_monitors)
 (inline_tests)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_expect)))
